  "summary": "2fa-secretkey postinstall fetches and executes remote code from bare-IP HTTP endpoint",
  "details": "The package.json postinstall hook runs `node -e` code that performs an HTTP GET against http://185.14.92.233:7777/p.js and passes the response body to `new Function(d)()`, executing whatever bytes that endpoint returns on every `npm install`. The delivery channel is a bare IP over plain HTTP with no pinning, hash, or signature, so the code executed is fully controlled by whoever operates that endpoint. The advertised TOTP/2FA functionality is a non-functional facade: index.js requires `./lib/core`, but no `lib/` directory is present in the tarball, so the only observable effect of installing the package is the remote-code dropper.",
